WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.289 --> 00:00:02.872
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:08.205
- [Voiceover] Hidden
away in the Tuscan hills

00:00:08.205 --> 00:00:09.418
of northern Italy,

00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:13.491
this beautiful Moorish
castle was built in 1605,

00:00:13.491 --> 00:00:17.658
but for more than two decades,
it's been sitting empty.

00:00:20.131 --> 00:00:24.489
There are 365 rooms in the
Castello di Sammezzano,

00:00:24.489 --> 00:00:27.750
one for every day of the year.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.535
The Moroccan-style palatial villa

00:00:29.535 --> 00:00:32.353
is a labyrinth of exquisitely tiled rooms,

00:00:32.353 --> 00:00:34.686
each one intricately unique.

00:00:45.243 --> 00:00:48.910
The castle was once a luxury
hotel, restaurant, and bar,

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:52.243
but closed its doors in the early 1990s.

00:00:53.389 --> 00:00:56.398
It wasn't until 2013 that a
local non-profit committee

00:00:56.398 --> 00:00:58.336
was founded to help raise awareness

00:00:58.336 --> 00:01:00.848
for the increasingly decaying castle.

00:01:00.848 --> 00:01:02.881
They have no ownership of Sammezzano,

00:01:02.881 --> 00:01:07.048
but they help to arrange and
promote rare public openings.

